# DEC-374 — environment isolation (do NOT drain the PRODUCTION budget in tests).
# The dev server (`npm run dev`) AND local E2E (Playwright launches `npm run dev`)
# talk to the STAGING sync worker, so WebSocket sockets held open while testing
# never burn the production Durable Objects duration budget.
#
# Safe by construction: Vite loads `.env.development` ONLY in `development` mode,
# so `npm run build` (production / Cloudflare Pages) ignores it and keeps the
# production default from `src/data/sync/config.ts`. This file is COMMITTED —
# never put a production secret here (the value below is a public worker URL).
VITE_SYNC_WORKER_URL=https://trippilot-sync-staging.trippilot.workers.dev
